rows=[]
for p in d['periods']:
 v=p['inputs'];rows.append(['FY'+str(p['fiscal_year']),b(v['ebit']),f'{D(v["tax_provision"])/D(v["pretax_income"])*100:.2f}%',b(v['da']),b(v['cash_ppe']),b(str(D(v['closing_nwc'])-D(v['opening_nwc']))),'<strong>'+b(p['fcff']['amount_usd'])+'</strong>','<a href="'+p['source_urls'][0]+'">Filing</a>'])
parts=['<h2>All five years available under one standardized method</h2><p>The missing FY2024–25 observations are resolved in the current platform by adopting an explicitly defined operating-income method across the entire FY2021–25 window. This is a source-derived standardized FCFF, not an audited Apple line item or an exact reconstruction of unlevered cash paid. The legacy CFO method and its two missing-interest gaps are preserved.</p>'+table(['FY','EBIT','Tax allocation','Reported D&A','Cash PP&E','Increase in defined NWC','Standardized FCFF','Source'],rows)]
parts+=['<h2>The eight implementation steps</h2>'+table(['Step','Treatment','Result'],[
['1. Define replacement','EBIT × (1 − reported provision / pretax) + reported combined D&A − cash PP&E − increase in defined current NWC','One method for all five years; no interest estimate'],
['2. Bind sources','Selected annual primary inline and extracted XBRL; 25 annual and 80 balance observations','Exact source dates, USD units, contexts, precision and hashes retained'],
['3. Tax allocation','Reported consolidated provision/pretax allocated to EBIT; actual current tax accruals retained in NWC consistently','Not exact operating cash taxes; no normalized forecast-tax change'],
['4. D&A','Use combined reported cash-statement D&A; retain SBC as an EBIT expense','No second depreciation addition and no $355M balancing plug'],
['5. Investment','Reported cash PP&E; finance principal not separately deducted; cash/noncash scope declared','No new financed assets or intangible investment guessed'],
['6. Working capital','Noncash/nondebt current balance convention; current operating/finance lease liabilities excluded','Six consecutive closing dates support five changes; no invented early-year tax split'],
['7. Reconcile methods','Exact new-versus-reported-cash-FCF bridges; legacy CFO values retained','Five zero-difference bridges, with differences explicitly explained'],
['8. Integrate and review','Overlay reaches catalog, DCF/scenario historical bars, Cash flows view and export','Independent source/arithmetic/runtime review and automated/browser checks recorded below']])]
parts+=['<h2>Important refinement: tax timing remains included</h2><p>The initial plan preferred separating income-tax balances from operating working capital. Source review found that FY2020–21 current tax balances are not separately disclosed. Removing tax only from later years would change the population mid-series. The implemented refinement retains current tax accruals inside the aggregate current-working-capital definition in every year. It is a documented modeling convention, not a claim that mixed captions are individually verified operating cash flows.</p><p><strong>Current tax payable increases by 17.782B in FY2024 and falls by 13.585B in FY2025.</strong> Those movements increase and decrease this series respectively. They are material and should be understood before using either year as a recurring forecast base. Removing current taxes where disclosed would change FY2024 to 97.898B and FY2025 to 108.709B; that tax-excluded series is not adopted because the early-year split is unavailable.</p>']
parts+=['<h2>Working-capital definition and six-date continuity</h2><div class="formula">NWC = current assets − cash − current marketable securities − current liabilities + commercial paper + current term debt + current finance-lease liability + current operating-lease liability</div><p>Other noncash current assets and nondebt current liabilities remain in the aggregate convention. This is a balance-sheet change model, not an assertion that the change is the exact reported cash-statement movement. It excludes noncurrent movements; it does not quietly assign an unexplained cash-flow residual to working capital.</p>'+table(['Date','Defined NWC'],[['2020-09-26',b(d['periods'][0]['inputs']['opening_nwc'])]]+[[p['identity']['annual_end'],b(p['inputs']['closing_nwc'])] for p in d['periods']])]
parts+=['<h2>D&A and investment qualifications remain visible</h2><p>For FY2024, later-note PP&E depreciation 8.2B plus intangible amortization 3.6B totals 11.8B, versus the cash-statement D&A 11.445B. The 0.355B difference remains unexplained. The adopted method deliberately uses the reported combined cash-statement population, consistently, and does not fill the difference. This is not certification of the broader expense-aligned economic-investment measure.</p><p>Cash PP&E is the stated investment perimeter. Noncash financed additions are not fabricated or double-counted; finance-lease principal is not a second capital-spending deduction. Exact expanded investment, intangible cash flows and lease timing remain separate analysis. <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019326000026/aapl-20260926.htm">Later comparative notes</a>.</p>']
parts+=['<h2>Why the old and new values differ</h2>'+table(['FY','Old CFO-based FCFF','New standardized FCFF','New minus reported CFO−PP&E'],[['FY'+str(p['fiscal_year']),b(p['legacy_cfo_fcff_usd']),b(p['new_standardized_fcff']['amount_usd']),b(p['new_minus_cash_fcf']['amount_usd'])] for p in old['periods']])+'<div class="formula">New FCFF − reported cash FCF = − allocated after-tax net nonoperating income − SBC − all other reported CFO adjustments − defined current NWC increase</div><p>All five bridges tie exactly using rational arithmetic. The “other CFO adjustments” are the actual retained source rows, not a balancing plug or a new pure-operating classification. The old CFO series retains SBC add-backs and a different cash/tax/investment population. The source bank and old projection are unchanged.</p>']
