parts+=['<h2>Validation</h2><pre>'+h(json.dumps(validation,indent=2))+'</pre><p><a href="independent-review/README.md">Independent review</a> · <a href="source-ledger.json">Source ledger</a> · <a href="adopted-history.json">Adopted calculations</a> · <a href="legacy-comparison.json">Exact method bridge</a> · <a href="decision.json">Decision and plan refinement</a></p>']
parts+=['<h2>What this resolves—and what it does not</h2><p><strong>Resolved:</strong> the current Apple historical FCFF display now has five source-derived values under one declared operating-income methodology, including FY2024 and FY2025. No missing interest was invented.</p><p>Apple’s overall financial review remains OPEN. Full FCFE financing classification, the stricter exact unlevered-cash reconstruction, broader D&A/investment alignment and per-share valuation are not certified by this scoped change. The old missing-interest observations remain null in the preserved legacy series. No Meta/Alphabet cash flow or forecast assumption is changed.</p><p>Method references: <a href="https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/free-cash-flow-valuation">CFA EBIT-based FCFF</a>; <a href="https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/New_Home_Page/valquestions/noncashwc.htm">Damodaran noncash/nondebt current working capital</a>. These support the framework, not a company-specific assertion that every Other balance is purely operating.</p>']
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'"><title>Apple historical FCFF remediation</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f1f5f7;color:#193b4e;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px 70px}h1{font:46px/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0}h2{font:28px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 18px}header{margin-bottom:28px}.flag{padding:18px;border-left:4px solid #aa862d;background:#fbf5e9}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}section{padding:26px;border:1px solid #dbe4ea;border-radius:10px;background:white;margin:20px 0}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}th,td{padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #dbe4ea;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#f2f6f9}a{color:#295e78}.formula{padding:16px;background:#f3f6f8;font:14px/1.7 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:13px}p{max-width:1100px}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:24px 12px}h1{font-size:34px}section{padding:18px 14px}table{min-width:620px}}</style></head><body><main><header><div class="eyebrow">Valuation Platform · Apple · FY2021–FY2025 · November 4, 2026</div><h1>Apple historical FCFF is available<br>under the adopted operating method</h1><p>FY2024 <strong>115.680B</strong> · FY2025 <strong>95.124B</strong></p><div class="flag"><strong>Available with disclosed methodology qualifications.</strong> The standardized five-year series is source-derived; it is not exact unlevered cash flow or full-company financial clearance. Current tax accruals are included uniformly. The original CFO series and its gaps remain traceable.</div></header>'''+''.join('<section>'+p+'</section>' for p in parts)+'</main></body></html>'
